The CLUT cache and the transfer state, for snapshots of the GS

A palette is copied from local memory when it is loaded (TEX0's CLD), and
the copy lives in the renderer's CLUT cache on the GPU. A game may draw
with a CLUT whose local memory has since been written, so a snapshot of
local memory and the registers does not hold it.

get_clut_snapshot reads the CLUT the shaders read now (1024 bytes: 512
16-bit entries) after a flush that waits for the GPU. set_clut_snapshot
writes one as a fresh instance of the cache and rewinds the cache to it,
which also drops every cached texture made with another CLUT.
transfer_idle says whether a HOST -> LOCAL transfer is half sent or a
LOCAL -> HOST one has words left to read, which a snapshot cannot hold.
Nothing else changes.

The port's mh2gs_state_get and mh2gs_state_set use them
(pc/gs/mh2gs.cpp). Applied by tools/setup.sh, tools/setup.ps1
and tools/pc/pgs_patches.py to the pinned paraLLEl-GS commit
(tools/versions.txt). paraLLEl-GS is LGPL-3.0-or-later; this patch is
published with the port under the same license.

